# Lines the g1-stack JOB LOG scan lets through its digit and card rules (bench-g1-stack.yml, job joblog-scan). Each line is a regular expression searched in a whole log line.
# One shape: a Go module download, `go: downloading <module path> <version>`, where the version is a pseudo-version (a 14-digit UTC timestamp and a 12-hex commit prefix). The timestamp joined with the
# separators reads as a 15-digit Luhn-valid number to the card rule (run 45128374794). The module path may hold no run of ten digits, and nothing may follow the version, so a number in the path,
# after the version or in any other line is still found; the secret, canary and JWT rules are not affected by this file.
^\S+Z go: downloading (?![^ ]*[0-9]{10})[A-Za-z0-9._/~-]+ v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+(-([0-9]+\.)?[0-9]{14}-[0-9a-f]{12})?(\+incompatible)?$
